CM_ "volvo_v40_2017_ptradar.dbc - Volvo V40 (C1, 2017) test DBC. Base: volvo_v40_2017_pt.dbc + Delphi ESR radar (bus 1) + findings from the 2026-11-08 drives (r1/r2/r3). REFERENCE ONLY: the code does not load this file. Bus map in the CSV logs: 0 = car/pt, 2 = camera, 1 = radar (Delphi ESR), 128/130 = panda echoes, 192/194 = OP tx. ID CLASH: 0x540 (1344) was NEW_MSG_1 on the car side in the base DBC; on bus 1 it is the radar Track_Sensor counter. The base NEW_MSG_1 (4|13@0+) was removed here, and the radar definition kept. Load radar messages with the radar bus only.";

CM_ BO_ 1280 "Radar track 1 (0x500). 0x500-0x53F = Target1..Target64, same layout, 20 Hz each, bus 1. In route 3 only ~39% of track-slot samples held a valid target; median 27 valid tracks per 50 ms frame (max 64). Most tracks are stationary scenery (closing speed median -6.5 m/s at own speed), so they must be filtered by the in-path IDs of 0x4E3 or by range/angle/width.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_STATUS "0 no target, 1 new, 2 new updated, 3 updated, 4 coasted, 5 merged, 6 invalid coasted, 7 new coasted (per Delphi ESR ICD, not verified on this car). Route 3 counts: 0 = 571k, 3 = 180k, 4 = 104k, 1 = 42k, 2 = 28k, 7 = 9k, 5 = 2k samples.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_RANGE "Range to track, 0.1 m steps. Route 3 valid tracks: 13 m (5th pct), 54 m (median), 162 m (95th pct).";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_RANGE_RATE "Closing speed, signed, 0.01 m/s. Negative = closing. Matches d(range)/dt with correlation 0.80 for the in-path lead (median error 0.7 m/s): usable but noisy.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_ANGLE "Azimuth, 0.1 deg. Valid tracks about -26 to +26 deg (5th/95th pct). Lead target median 0.1 deg.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_WIDTH "Track width, 0.5 m steps. Median 0.5 m.";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_LAT_RATE "Lateral rate, 0.25 steps (unit unverified).";
CM_ SG_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_RANGE_ACCEL "Range acceleration, 0.05 m/s^2. Not yet checked against the lead.";
CM_ BO_ 1344 "0x540, bus 1, ~200 Hz, 8 bytes. Byte 0 is a rolling counter 0..9, bytes 1-7 constant 0x0A in r3. The ESR DBC lists this ID as Track_Sensor with 1 byte; actual DLC here is 8. Probably a track/scan sequence counter, no sensor data.";
CM_ SG_ 1344 CAN_TX_TRACK_ROLLING_COUNT_2 "Original ESR DBC bit (4|1). In r3 the whole of byte 0 counts 0..9; see Track_Counter.";
CM_ SG_ 1344 Track_Counter "Byte 0, counts 0..9 and wraps (r3, first 12 frames: 01 02 ... 09 00 01 02). Added from the 2026-11-08 log.";
CM_ BO_ 1251 "0x4E3, bus 1, 20 Hz. The radar's own in-path target selection. Byte 1 (PATH_ID_ACC_MOVE) and byte 7 (PATH_ID_ACC_STAT) hold the track ID (1..64, 0 = none) of the moving / stationary ACC target. In r3 while stock ACC was in tracking state (0x30 byte 7 = 0x8F) the radar named an in-path moving target in 96% of frames (29% with ACC in standby). Bytes 2 and 4 (CMBB_MOVE, FCW_MOVE) carry nearly the same IDs as byte 1 in r3. Bytes 3 and 5 are mostly 0 (stationary IDs for CMBB/FCW).";
CM_ SG_ 1251 CAN_TX_PATH_ID_ACC_MOVE "Track ID of the moving in-path target used by ACC (0 = none). Most common IDs in r3: 0 (8454 frames), 61, 12, 14, 2, 8. Changes about every 8 s while tracking (20 changes in 164 s). Lead while tracking: range median 27.1 m (11 to 47 m), closing -0.7 m/s (-2.7 to +0.9), time gap 2.8 s (1.8 to 3.6 s).";
CM_ SG_ 1251 CAN_TX_PATH_ID_ACC_STAT "Track ID of the stationary in-path target for ACC (0 = none). Set only ~2% of the time while tracking in r3, so stopped-car behaviour is not covered by this log.";
CM_ SG_ 1251 CAN_TX_PARTIAL_BLOCKAGE "Stayed 0 for the whole drive: no radar blockage fault.";
CM_ SG_ 1251 CAN_TX_TRUCK_TARGET_DET "Truck target detected flag. Not examined.";
CM_ BO_ 1248 "0x4E0 ESR_Status, bus 1, 20 Hz.";
CM_ BO_ 1249 "0x4E1 ESR_Status2, bus 1, 20 Hz. Contains radar faults (internal, overheat, range-performance, comm error) and temperature. Check these first after install: none were examined in r3 beyond partial blockage.";
CM_ BO_ 1250 "0x4E2 ESR_SW, bus 1, 20 Hz. Software/hardware version and serial number: useful to identify the radar unit (Delphi ESR).";
CM_ BO_ 1264 "0x4F0 Vehicle_Data, bus 1, 50 Hz. Sent TO the radar (speed, yaw rate, steering angle, curvature). The radar needs vehicle speed and yaw to pick the in-path target. Speed unit here is m/s x 0.0625.";
CM_ BO_ 1265 "0x4F1 SensorInput, bus 1, 50 Hz. Sent TO the radar (mounting offset, misalignment, max tracks, grouping mode, wiper status, etc.).";
CM_ BO_ 1488 "0x5D0, bus 1, 20 Hz in r3. Defined in the ESR DBC (valid long-range track data). Not analysed.";
CM_ BO_ 1489 "0x5D1, bus 1, 20 Hz in r3. Defined in the ESR DBC (valid mid-range track data). Not analysed.";
CM_ BO_ 1508 "0x5E4, bus 1, 20 Hz in r3. Defined in the ESR DBC as AD_Data. Not analysed.";
CM_ "Bus 1 IDs seen in r3 that are NOT defined here or in ESR.dbc: 0x5E5-0x5E9 and 0x5F2, 0x5F4 (20 Hz each), 0x5B0-0x5B8 and 0x5BC-0x5BE (0.5 Hz each). Likely radar debug/diagnostic frames. Not analysed.";

CM_ SG_ 352 ACC_AccelRequest "NEW (replaces NEW_SIGNAL_2 56|7@1+). Byte 7 of 0x160 = stock ACC acceleration request. 192 counts is about 0 m/s^2, below = braking, above = acceleration. Fit 0.066 m/s^2 per count (raw = 192 + accel/0.066), correlation ~0.9 with measured acceleration, leads it by 0.2-0.4 s. The older WIPACCv40 estimate was 0.0556 / -10.72. Route 3 braking example: ego 49 to 5 km/h, lead 48 to 13 m, request down to about -1.4 m/s^2, then +1.1 m/s^2. Read it from bus 2 (camera original): on bus 0 with OP active it is a sparse constant 191.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_2_b7_6 "Frame-type tag: 3 on the full (main) frames, 0 on the ~20% alternate (masked) frames. Main frames carry real data; alternate frames repeat the shape with Byte_3 about 18-21.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_3 "Main frames (tag 3): 70-100 = measured acceleration feedback. Alternate frames about 18-21. Drifts 84 -> 83 -> 82 during ACC braking.";
CM_ SG_ 352 Byte_2_b4_0 "Route dependent (21 / 29 / 30 / 8-31 seen); not a counter. Byte 2 idle 213, 245 once ACC braking starts (only bit 5, ACC_BrakeRequest, differs).";

CM_ SG_ 48 ACCStatusActive "Old signal name. See byte 7 of 0x30 on bus 2 (camera original; bus 0 shows 0x88 while OP is active): 0x88 off, 0x8A standby, 0x8E active no lead, 0x8F active tracking a lead, 0x9x same states with the time-gap pulse bit set.";
CM_ SG_ 432 BrakeStatus "Byte 2 bits 0-2 of 0x1B0 (bus 0, ~50 Hz). Raw byte 2 seen on 2026-11-08: 0xA0 idle (also pedal presses, ACC off), 0xA5 = ACC braking (5), 0xA1 = 1 seen just before/after an ACC braking event, 0xE1 / 0xE0 = ACC holding the car at standstill (bit 6 set; value 1 or 0). The pedal never produced 0xA5. ACC braking trips the 0x55 pressure bits (24 and 38), which makes OP see brakePressed and disengage. volvo.h and carstate.py ignore the pressure bits while BrakeStatus == 5. NOTE: an earlier version of this comment used a shifted (bits 2-4) reading and called ACC braking 1; the DBC signal here (value 5) was right.";
VAL_ 432 BrakeStatus 0 "None" 1 "ACC hold or transition (0xA1 / 0xE1)" 5 "ACC braking (0xA5)" ;
CM_ BO_ 85 "0x55 PedalandBrake. Bits 24 and 38 are pressure thresholds that ACC braking also trips. OP carstate brakePressed = BrakePedalActive2 or BrakePedalActive; panda volvo.h also sets brake_pressed from bits 24/38 for C1. This is why stock ACC braking disengages OP. Do NOT use these bits to detect the driver pedal while ACC is on.";
VAL_ 1264 CAN_RX_YAW_RATE_VALIDITY 1 "Valid" 0 "Invalid" ;
VAL_ 1264 CAN_RX_VEHICLE_SPEED_DIRECTION 1 "Reverse" 0 "Forward" ;
VAL_ 1264 CAN_RX_STEERING_VALIDITY 1 "True" 0 "False" ;
VAL_ 1264 CAN_RX_STEERING_ANGLE_SIGN 1 "Right Clockwise" 0 "Left CounterClockwise" ;
VAL_ 1264 CAN_RX_STEERING_ANGLE_RATE_SIGN 1 "Right Clockwise" 0 "Left CounterClockwise" ;
VAL_ 1280 CAN_TX_TRACK_STATUS 0 "No target" 1 "New target" 2 "New updated target" 3 "Updated target" 4 "Coasted target" 5 "Merged target" 6 "Invalid coasted target" 7 "New coasted target" ;
CM_ SG_ 432 BrakeHold "Byte 2 bit 6 of 0x1B0. Set (0xE0/0xE1) while stock ACC holds the car at standstill. Only seen with ACC active. volvo.h and carstate.py treat it as ACC-owned braking while ACC is active.";
